\ `see` steps over every operand, and prints literals that read back.
\
\ The decompiler advanced one cell past any opcode it had no case for, so
\ the inline string of `."` / `abort"`, and the word pointer carried by a
\ reference to a constant, array, created, deferred or DOES> word, were
\ decoded as opcodes: it printed whichever word first had the same
\ runtime, then garbage - or crashed when string bytes looked like NEST.
\ String and real literals didn't round-trip either (a stray leading
\ space; 1.0 printed as the integer 1).

10 constant ten
5 array arr
create buf 4 allot
defer hook
: noop ;
' noop is hook
: const create , does> @ ;
3 const three

: shout ." "Hi, \"you\"!\n" ;
: guard abort" "no\tway" ;
: refs ten 2 arr ! buf hook three + ;
: lits "a\\b" 1.0 0.5 -2.25e-3 ;

see shout
see guard
see refs
see lits
